keywords:
  - SEC
  - EDGAR
  - 8-K
  - corporate events
  - data breach disclosure
  - executive changes
  - mergers and acquisitions
  - IPO
  - proxy statements
  - auditor changes
  - financial statements
  - forecast calibration
  - prediction intervals
  - primary source
abstract: >
  Twelve boards built from United States SEC filings on the day they are filed, one per 8-K item or form the filer declared,
  plus a company card for every filer on the boards (about 3,000) read from its own audited XBRL facts in the style of an
  actuarial report, and a forecast ledger in which every 80% revenue range is hashed before the outcome is known and scored
  when the next annual report arrives. Nothing in the boards is written or inferred; every row links its filing on sec.gov.
  Refreshed every business day. Free to use with credit to POPS4 under CC BY 4.0.
